<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Chapter 47 — Observability Fundamentals.
    events/       WideEvent and WideEventWriter: one structured event per request, every field that might explain it
    correlation/  TraceParent: the W3C traceparent header that joins spans, logs, events and exemplars
    sampling/     TraceIdRatio (head sampling, as the OpenTelemetry SDK decides) and TailPolicy (after the fact)
    analysis/     BubbleUp: what differs about the bad requests, from any fields, without knowing in advance
    resources/    the gateway OpenTelemetry Collector, Prometheus with RED recording rules, the Java agent's
                  settings and a Spring Boot 4 service's OpenTelemetry export
  verify/run.sh runs FoodFleet's checkout services under the OpenTelemetry Java agent 2.32.0 with a Collector 0.162.0,
  Prometheus 3.15.0 and JDK Flight Recorder: finding a gray failure with each signal, what each costs, instrumentation
  overhead, profiling, and cardinality.
-->
